* {{audio|en|En-us-somewhat.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|some|what}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# To a limited extent or degree; not [[completely]].
#: {{syn|en|a bit|a touch|only just|Thesaurus:moderately|Thesaurus:slightly}}
#: {{ant|en|absolutely|quite|wholly|totally|Thesaurus:completely}}
#: {{cot|en|rather}}
#: {{ux|en|The crowd was '''somewhat''' larger than expected, perhaps due to the good weather.}}
#: {{ux|en|The decision to shave or not is a '''somewhat''' personal one.}}
#: {{ux|en|The searing heat cooled '''somewhat''' as the sun set in the evening.}}
#: {{ux|en|That hat seems '''somewhat''' small for him.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=2|passage=I had occasion {{...}} to make a '''somewhat''' long business trip to Chicago, and on my return {{...}} I found Farrar awaiting me in the railway station. He smiled his wonted fraction by way of greeting, {{...}} and finally leading me to his buggy, turned and drove out of town. I was completely mystified at such an unusual proceeding.}}
#* {{RQ:Grew Plants|passage=its taste, which is plainly acid, and '''somewhat''' rough}}
# {{rfv-sense|en}} {{lb|en|UK|meiosis}} [[very|Very]].
#: {{syn|en|a bit|absolutely|ever so|quite|Thesaurus:very}}
#: {{ant|en|a touch|only just|scarcely|Thesaurus:slightly}}
#: {{ux|en|That hat seems '''somewhat''' small for him.}}<!--the ironic tone cannot be written down here; this is an example of the theme that occasionally a ux works for more than one sense of a word.-->
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1942|month=September and October|title=Notes and News: Lynton & Barnstaple Stock|journal=Railway Magazine|page=309|text=Two of the coaches are still on the site of the line; one, a first class observation coach carrying the S.R. number 6991, is at Snapper Halt, where it still stands, in fair condition but '''somewhat''' weatherbeaten {{...}}}}

