{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁em-}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|xno|-}} {{m|fro|resumer}}, {{der|en|frm|resumer}}, from {{der|en|la|resumere}}, from {{m|la|re-}} + {{m|la|sumere||to take}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|en|RP}}
** {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈzjuːm/|a=non-<<yod-coalescence>>}} {{enPR|rĭzyo͞om'}}
*** {{audio|en|en-uk-resume.ogg|a=UK}}
** {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈʒum/|/ɹəˈʒum/|a=yod-coalescence}}
* {{a|en|GA}}
** {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈzum/|/ɹəˈzum/|a=yod-dropping}}
*** {{audio|en|en-us-resume.ogg|a=California}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈzjʉːm/|a=AU}}
** {{audio|en|en-au-resume.ogg|a=Queensland}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːm|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|re|sume}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|now|_|rare}} To [[take back]] possession of (something) {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|regain}}
#: {{ux|en|Ladies and gentlemen, please '''resume''' your seats.}}
#* {{RQ:Richardson Clarissa|letter=28|text=As to the advice you give, to '''resume''' my estate, I am determined not to litigate with my father, let what will be the consequence to myself.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1974|author=w:Lawrence Durrell|title=Monsieur|page=8|publisher=Faber & Faber|year_published=1992
|passage=For after that initiation it was impossible to attach any profound importance to the notion of dying. All individual deaths had been '''resumed''' by the death of God!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Geoff Moore|title=Essential Real Property|publisher=Cavendish Publishing|isbn=1876905174|page=116
|passage=By resumption The Government, most likely the State Government, can '''resume''' property for the purposes of building a road or a school or some other purpose.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|now|_|rare}} To [[summarise]]. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1974|author=w:Lawrence Durrell|title=Monsieur|page=36|publisher=Faber & Faber|year_published=1992
|passage=He {{...}} used to say that each separate death had taught him something new about death, and that he was going to '''resume''' this knowledge in a philosophic essay about dying.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To start (something) again that has been [[stop]]ped or [[pause]]d from the point at which it was stopped or paused; [[continue]], [[carry on]]. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#: {{ant|en|suspend}}
#: {{ux|en|We will '''resume''' this discussion tomorrow at nine.}}
